## CRIT-1 — Action Required From You (Git History Purge)

This requires rewriting git history and must be coordinated manually. Steps:

```bash
# Install BFG (if not already)
brew install bfg

# From project root — run AFTER committing all current changes
git gc --prune=now

# Purge .env from all commits
bfg --delete-files .env

# Clean up reflogs
git reflog expire --expire=now --all
git gc --prune=now --aggressive

# Force push
git push --force
```

> **Also:** Rotate the Gemini API key in [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials) and update `backend/.env` with the new key. The old key `AIzaSyAVtbrZWAYIivLzygrHfKMsQYB4DG5M35A` is still visible in git history until you run BFG.
